# Review requirement for the trust surface (2026-08-18 adversarial review,
# finding P1-1).
#
# The finding: the sole required branch-protection check (`ci`) is reported by
# a workflow that pull requests can rewrite, with zero required reviews and
# auto-merge enabled -- so one self-greening PR can void every gate. The same
# hole exists one level down for the gate scripts themselves: a PR that edits
# `scripts/check_*.py` to exit 0 neuters that gate inside a green `ci`.
#
# This file is INERT until branch protection (or a ruleset) enables it:
#   Settings -> Branches -> main -> "Require a pull request before merging"
#   -> "Require review from Code Owners" (requires >= 1 approving review).
# With that enabled, a PR touching any path below cannot merge -- auto-merge
# included -- until a code owner approves it. PRs touching only library code
# under DerivedAlgGeo/ are unaffected.
#
# OPERATIONAL CAVEAT, single-maintainer repo: GitHub forbids approving your
# own PR. If agent PRs are opened by the owner account, enabling code-owner
# review makes trust-surface PRs unmergeable by that account alone. The
# working arrangements are: open agent PRs from a machine account or GitHub
# App so the owner reviews them, or scope the requirement to a ruleset with a
# bypass list the owner uses deliberately. Choose one BEFORE flipping the
# setting.

# CI workflows and this file: the P1-1 core. Whoever edits the required
# check's definition must not be the only party who looked at the edit.
